{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review of the entire patent application draft. The review traced every claim limitation, numbered part, and substantive description in the draft and figure briefs to the affirmative inventor disclosure in `input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`. The draft was also checked for internal consistency.\n\nThe claims, description, and most figure briefs are well-supported by the inventor's disclosure and internally consistent. However, a critical issue was found in the drawing instructions for the cam ring. The brief for FIG. 3, which purports to show the complete cam ring, omits the three oblique slots that are essential to its disclosed function of synchronizing the jaw carriages. This makes the figure inconsistent with the disclosure, the claims, and other parts of the description. A fix is provided to add the missing slots to the figure brief. After this correction, the application should be ready for filing."}
